# `GENRE-CONNECTOR-SPELLING`/`GENRE-NODE-SPELLING` applied a FOURTH time. A word this genre spells
# differently is not an unknown word, and the diagnostic says which word and
# why. Both directions, in two sections:
#   `node` and `edge` under `sequence`   -> write `lifeline` / `message`
#   `lifeline` and `message` under `block` -> write `node` / `edge`
# There is no version gate on either spelling, unlike `flowline`: the GENRE
# requires figdown 0.4, so neither word is reachable from an earlier document.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
node x "X"
edge c -> x

figdown 0.1 block
node a "A"
node b "B"
lifeline l "L"
message a -> b
